```

## Local Model

```text
Model: Llama 3.2
Parameters: 3.2B
Context Length: 131072 tokens
Embedding Length: 3072
Quantization: Q4_K_M
```

## Core LLM Pipeline

```text
Text
 ↓
Tokenization
 ↓
Token IDs
 ↓
Embeddings
 ↓
Transformer Blocks
 ↓
Self-Attention
 ↓
Output Logits
 ↓
Next-Token Selection
 ↓
Generated Text
```

## Key Takeaways

* LLMs process text as tokens.
* Parameters are learned numerical values inside the model.
* Pre-training teaches general language patterns through next-token prediction.
* Training updates model parameters; inference uses the trained parameters.
* Transformers use attention to model relationships between tokens.
* LLM generation happens through repeated next-token prediction.
* Quantization reduces model storage/memory requirements and can improve local inference efficiency.
* A local LLM can be run without an external API key using Ollama.
